## Rebase conflict resolution (2026-09-21, onto main 373bc9f92)
This commit conflicted with upstream d9eb42db11 "feat(sglang): support cache salt routing (#14803)" in lib/kv-router/src/zmq_wire/deserialize.rs, two hunks in the positional `visit_seq` BlockStored path. Main replaced the positional `lora_name` read with an untagged `BlockStoredNamespace { LoraName(String) | SglangMetadata { cache_salt } }` and made `cache_namespace` prefer that slot over extra_keys. This commit keeps `lora_id` alive (main discards it) and computes `shared_cache_eligible` from lora_id, lora_name, block_mm_infos, extra_keys, and cache_namespace. Resolution: keep both enums (`BlockStoredNamespace` and `ProvenanceField`), keep main's namespace match and `cache_namespace.or_else(...)`, then run our eligibility computation on the derived `lora_name` / `cache_namespace`. SGLang cache-salted stores are therefore eligible (extra_keys is None, so `extra_keys_are_text_only` is true), which is correct: a text-only salted prefix is still text-only. Verified: zmq_wire suite 66 tests including main's new `test_deserialize_sglang_cache_salt`; kv-router 1074; llm kv_router/mooncake/preprocessor 652.
